{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/3999-god-machine-lineage","id":3999,"title":"God-Machine Lineage","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-05T21:23:23-08:00","id":3999,"title":"God-Machine Lineage","content":"For my new campaign I am taking a crack at writing up a Lineage that ties Promethean's into the machinations of the God-Machine. It was inspired by the quite cool NPCs presented in Saturnine Nights who were each made by a different kind of supernatural being. It's pretty barebones right now because, despite liking the concept, I'm not sure exactly how to execute it. I think much of this could change before I'm done. I'd love feedback as I'm hoping to make this Lineage available to my PCs if it is hammered out.<br /> <div align=\"center\"><u><b>Seraphim</b></u></div> <br /> <b>Progenitor:</b> Created in modern nights, the Demiurge responsible for the Seraphim may still be alive in the world. During the brief time the first Seraphim knew his Demiurge he was told only that his Demiurge was himself a divine being who had disobeyed God and sought to make one of his own kind for succor.<br /> <br /> <b>Other Nicknames:</b> The Blessed<br /> <br /> <b>Appearance:</b> Though there are few Seraphim in the world, all are Unfleshed.<br /> <br /> <b>Humour:</b> The ruling humour of the Seraphim is unique to their Lineage, <i>manna</i>. Imbued with the divine nature of their demiurge, Seraphim are prone to seeing patterns where others see chaos, fate where others see coincidence, and suffer from frequent bursts of moral outrage against a world that does not meet their stringent standards. The unusual humour drives some Seraphim to be martyrs just as much as it drives others to be relentless judges.<br /> <br /> <b>Element:</b> Seraphim are not associated with a particular element. They regain a point of Pyros when they rest amongst functioning complex machines (sleeping in a running car, in front of a TV that\u2019s turned on, or surrounded by personal electronic devices).<br /> <br /> <b>Bestowment:</b> No idea.<br /> <br /> <b>Torment:</b> When suffering through the throes of Torment, the Seraphim cast righteous judgment on themselves and others. If the Seraphim has judged himself to be wicked or morally failing, this Torment might involve self-flagellation, attempting to make amends (no matter the cost to him or others) to those he believes he has wronged, or long periods of retreat from the world. If he judges others it may involve inflicting whatever the Seraphim has decided is an appropriate judgment on the individual or individuals.<br /> <br /> <b>Disquiet:</b> Mortals suffering from the Disquiet of the Seraphim believe themselves to be superior to others, most especially the irritatingly holier-than-thou Seraphim. Early stages look like cold disregard or curt disapprovals of the Seraphim while later levels involve fanatical witch hunts to correct perceived wrongs committed by the Seraphim.<br /> <br /> <b>Wasteland:</b> Their mechanical nature colors the effect Seraphim have on the world around them. While plants whither, advanced thinking life begins acting in more and more predictable patterns. Technology seems to work even better than normal at earlier levels but as Wasteland advances the technology becomes glitch and performs functions it should not be able to (PCs will link with various secure and insecure networks it should have no access to, cell phones will begin making calls or financial transactions, microwaves will self-start and combust, etc.).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/806-benjamin-beard","name":"Benjamin Beard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar806_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T16:13:59-08:00","id":4693,"title":"","content":"If you want to tie them closer to the god-machine, give them the element of order, so in places where things happen as they should with efficiency, they regain pyros.<br /> <br /> Likewise, you could make the disquiet paranoia, people begin thinking that their choices were laid out before them, their free will is gone, and it's all the seraphim's fault.<br /> <br /> Self Righteousness isn't really right for their godmachine origins, I'd make it judgement based on perfection, not morality. Failure in general, not wickedness which the godmachine couldn't care less about.<br /> <br /> As for bestowment, I'd go with spare parts the alternate frankenstein bestowment for repairing or tinkering with themselves with machine parts, the scrutiny to make them prophets sort of, or ephemeral flesh since angels are a form of ephemeral being. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-10T00:35:08-08:00","id":7215,"title":"","content":"One of the more intriguing notions, I'll give you.<br /> <br /> Being creatures born of a rational, cosmic machine, perhaps their humour is something less alchemical: spinal fluid. Or, homeostatic pressure, the result of a system in balance with itself, in organic form. Maybe it's gangrene, because the Promethean is meant as a means of shunting off entropy and heat from the Machine itself. Or Aether, as the case may be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-15T17:37:37-08:00","id":11726,"title":"","content":"Random thought inspired by your Lineage write up: What if the core lineages are the result of the God-Machine (the use of spare parts) while Extempore (having no maker) are the &quot;real&quot; lineages of the Principle?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/237-dagcon-faraday","name":"Dagcon Faraday","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-15T19:38:25-08:00","id":11800,"title":"","content":"I still plan on coming back to this Lineage as I want to include it in my upcoming game but life has gotten in the way of me returning to it as quickly as I had hoped. I definitely appreciate the thoughts and feedback!<br /> <br /> When I sat down to write the Lineage I knew (and still know) very little about the upcoming Demons from D:tD and I think I was trying to find some way to blend more traditional angelic attributes with those I surmised or guessed would be included in Demon. I think it's led to a concept that is maybe is not refined enough. I am going to focus in on the God-Machine specific lore and try to bring it in around that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/806-benjamin-beard","name":"Benjamin Beard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar806_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-19T01:17:14-08:00","id":13854,"title":"","content":"Well you could always make two lineages, there are judeo-christian angels in the nwod, they just don't work for the god-machine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-20T16:54:31-08:00","id":14973,"title":"","content":"I\u2019d want to make the Lineage considerably older than you posit: the God-Machine has been around since before even the Nameless Empire featured in <b>Mummy</b> (if there\u2019s any truth to the Pain Prophet\u2019s ramblings). I could see making two \u201cparallel Lineages\u201d that differ primarily in that one of them is Unfleshed (and associated with the God-Machine) while the other one isn\u2019t. More thoughts later; I\u2019ve been called in to work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-20T22:43:31-08:00","id":15150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/3999-god-machine-lineage?p=14973#post14973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019d want to make the Lineage considerably older than you posit: the God-Machine has been around since before even the Nameless Empire featured in <b>Mummy</b> (if there\u2019s any truth to the Pain Prophet\u2019s ramblings). I could see making two \u201cparallel Lineages\u201d that differ primarily in that one of them is Unfleshed (and associated with the God-Machine) while the other one isn\u2019t. More thoughts later; I\u2019ve been called in to work.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is a pretty interesting idea...and they wouldn't even have to be parallel. The God-Machine was constructed from advanced machinery since time immemorial so it would be interesting if they existed as a kind of proto-Unfleshed. Unfleshed before human technology was ever capable of it but using broken and busted pieces of God-Machine infrastructure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/806-benjamin-beard","name":"Benjamin Beard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar806_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T01:02:18-08:00","id":15220,"title":"","content":"Are you aware of the construct prometheans, Benjamin? That prometheans can be made from ivory, wood, silver, steel, iron, etc? Or partially made from such things, nothing stops a promethean from being mostly flesh but having leather skin and metal bones.<br /> <br /> Perhaps the lineage used to be made from human flesh and metal, evolving into an unfleshed lineage as technology started to catch up with the god-machine? Demon forms tend towards the biomechanical, and they're supposed to be reflections of their past forms as angels, so a god-machine lineage being biomechanical would make sense to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-23T12:09:17-08:00","id":16722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/3999-god-machine-lineage?p=15220#post15220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you aware of the construct prometheans, Benjamin? That prometheans can be made from ivory, wood, silver, steel, iron, etc? Or partially made from such things, nothing stops a promethean from being mostly flesh but having leather skin and metal bones.<br /> <br /> Perhaps the lineage used to be made from human flesh and metal, evolving into an unfleshed lineage as technology started to catch up with the god-machine? Demon forms tend towards the biomechanical, and they're supposed to be reflections of their past forms as angels, so a god-machine lineage being biomechanical would make sense to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>For reference sake, I believe the correspondences go something like:<br /> <br /> &lt;Lineage: Humour (Element) = Favored Construct Material&gt;<br /> <br /> Frankenstein: Choleric (Fire) = Copper<br /> Galatea: Sanguine (Air) = Marble<br /> Osiris: Phlegmatic (Water) = Limestone<br /> Tammuz: Melancholic (Earth) = Clay<br /> Ulgan: Ectoplasmic (Spirit) = Birch<br /> <br /> Zeka: Any humour (as long as its radioactive)<br /> Unfleshed: Any or none (technology-based with no human &quot;parts&quot;)<br /> <br /> Could Unfleshed possibly be the construct version of the Zeky?<br /> <br /> Or...the Zeka have a Construct version dealing with irradiated materials and the Unfleshed might have a &quot;body parts&quot; counterpart. This could open up an opportunity a &quot;god-machine&quot; lineage and the Unfleshed being constructs thereof, in which case the humour could be = &quot;any as so long as its fabricated&quot;<br /> <br /> A morgue could be &quot;infrastructure&quot; used to pull off an occult matrix of the generative act..or ...maybe a cloning facility actually being used for the covers of Angels..hmm<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/237-dagcon-faraday","name":"Dagcon Faraday","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-23T16:07:25-08:00","id":16850,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/3999-god-machine-lineage?p=15220#post15220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you aware of the construct prometheans, Benjamin? That prometheans can be made from ivory, wood, silver, steel, iron, etc? Or partially made from such things, nothing stops a promethean from being mostly flesh but having leather skin and metal bones.<br /> <br /> Perhaps the lineage used to be made from human flesh and metal, evolving into an unfleshed lineage as technology started to catch up with the god-machine? Demon forms tend towards the biomechanical, and they're supposed to be reflections of their past forms as angels, so a god-machine lineage being biomechanical would make sense to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, yeah, I really like that. I'm going to basically completely rewrite this now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/806-benjamin-beard","name":"Benjamin Beard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar806_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-23T16:38:47-08:00","id":16864,"title":"","content":"Recall that the Unfleshed are electromechanical, with an illusory shell that makes it look human. Regular Prometheans are composed entirely of flesh. I think that if any Lineage would be suitable to straddle the gulf (part flesh, part mechanical; and it\u2019s hard to tell where one begins and the other ends), it would be one whose demiurge was an agent of the God-Machine. <br /> <br /> Also bear in mind that clockwork is ancient, and the Divine Fire is notorious for making otherwise-impossible things possible. I see no reason why the Lineage in question couldn\u2019t be as old as dirt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-05T10:11:32-08:00","id":23817,"title":"","content":"I like the idea you've got here, but I think I would do it very differently. Just off the top of my head:<br /> <br /> <u><b>The Lazares</b></u><br /> <b>Element:</b> Aether; Pyros is recovered by sleeping before a TV showing static, or to the sound of white noise, or beneath the aurora.<br /> <b>Humour:</b> Cerebrospinal fluid, granted an appropriately mystic name; Swedenborg's &quot;spirituous lymph&quot; might suffice.<br /> <b>Torment:</b> Paranoid schizophrenia, more or less. The Lazarus sees sinister patterns in everything, and percieves himself as the victim (or, perhaps, the hand) of conspiracy. Ominous hallucinations are common.<br /> <b>Disquiet:</b> Similar to the Torment, in that it causes paranoia and the perception of omens. It's subtler, though (no hallucinations), and tends to seed seemingly inexplicable social groups in the affected community; all the local adulterers might form a clique, even though none of them know about the others' adultery.<br /> <b>Wasteland:</b> Yours is very good, so I'm keeping it. I could see there being some minor temporal anomalies during the last stage, though.<br /> <b>Disfigurements:</b> The Lazares are quasi-Unfleshed, so their disfigurements are the mechanisms (functional or otherwise) integrated into their flesh. Some are almost entirely mechanical, with only the CSF and maybe some token organic matter (like an eye, or teeth, or a whole hand) to separate them from the truly mechanical.<br /> <b>Bestowment:</b> I'm thinking that it should be some kind of bonuses to perception checks, as well as Computer and Investigation. It would manifest as a weaker, beneficial form of their Torment, making them very aware of patterns and capable of surprisingly accurate leaps of logic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":97,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","user":"The MG","date":". 12-06-2013, 03:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T13:56:49-08:00","id":24624,"title":"","content":"Bestowment: Neo-Sight? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T17:38:46-08:00","id":24777,"title":"","content":"One part Neo-Sight, one part Sherlock Scan, and one part Stanky Old Wizard Eyes, with a touch of Divine Revelation for flavour.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T19:57:08-08:00","id":24848,"title":"","content":"\u2026So, Mage Sight? :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-08T15:00:44-08:00","id":26070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/3999-god-machine-lineage?p=23817#post23817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the idea you've got here, but I think I would do it very differently. Just off the top of my head:<br /> <br /> <u><b>The Lazares</b></u><br /> <b>Element:</b> Aether; Pyros is recovered by sleeping before a TV showing static, or to the sound of white noise, or beneath the aurora.<br /> <b>Humour:</b> Cerebrospinal fluid, granted an appropriately mystic name; Swedenborg's &quot;spirituous lymph&quot; might suffice.<br /> <b>Torment:</b> Paranoid schizophrenia, more or less. The Lazarus sees sinister patterns in everything, and percieves himself as the victim (or, perhaps, the hand) of conspiracy. Ominous hallucinations are common.<br /> <b>Disquiet:</b> Similar to the Torment, in that it causes paranoia and the perception of omens. It's subtler, though (no hallucinations), and tends to seed seemingly inexplicable social groups in the affected community; all the local adulterers might form a clique, even though none of them know about the others' adultery.<br /> <b>Wasteland:</b> Yours is very good, so I'm keeping it. I could see there being some minor temporal anomalies during the last stage, though.<br /> <b>Disfigurements:</b> The Lazares are quasi-Unfleshed, so their disfigurements are the mechanisms (functional or otherwise) integrated into their flesh. Some are almost entirely mechanical, with only the CSF and maybe some token organic matter (like an eye, or teeth, or a whole hand) to separate them from the truly mechanical.<br /> <b>Bestowment:</b> I'm thinking that it should be some kind of bonuses to perception checks, as well as Computer and Investigation. It would manifest as a weaker, beneficial form of their Torment, making them very aware of patterns and capable of surprisingly accurate leaps of logic.</div> </div> </div> </div>I definitely like this direction. Where did you get the name Lazares from? Do you have an idea for a myth already in existence that could provide the history for this Lineage or is the Lineage so obscure that humans have no myths about them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/806-benjamin-beard","name":"Benjamin Beard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar806_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-09T19:05:58-08:00","id":26906,"title":"","content":"Lazarus: a friend of Jesus who died a premature death and whom Jesus resurrected. It isn\u2019t the first instance of this happening in the Bible (that one involves the prophet Elijah restoring life to the son of a widow who had taken care of him); but aside from Jesus\u2019 own \u201cself-resurrection\u201d, it\u2019s by far the most famous.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T16:25:50-08:00","id":28370,"title":"","content":"The name does indeed derive from Lazarus of Bethany. It seemed appropriate, though I now cannot figure out where I got that plural form from.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Benjamin Beard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/3999-god-machine-lineage?p=26070#post26070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you have an idea for a myth already in existence that could provide the history for this Lineage or is the Lineage so obscure that humans have no myths about them?</div> </div> </div> </div>I hadn't thought about it, honestly. My gut feeling is to go with the obscurity thing, but present a bunch of contradictory and vaguely conspiratorial origins, to go with the tenor of the God-Machine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T14:13:35-07:00","id":943860,"title":"","content":"Wait, wrong thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","user":"Leliel","date":". 08-04-2016, 05:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T18:12:24-07:00","id":944034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a